Z||000000||Mark Matthews||12-01-2001||07:40 AM||||Okay, so as far as fibarglass quality goes, how's the stuff from PISA?  I've thought about doing some to my old BMW, but the BMW forum told me to do at as a last resort.  Does their stuff hold up pretty well?  Is there anything you can do to sturdy it up?<P>This my sound totally off, but I'm just thinking out loud here.  I did order a glass body kit for my BMW but the stuff was paper  thin and damaged, returned it and got full refund.  If it hadn't come damaged I may have used it, if I could have made it stronger.  Is adding you're own layers of glass to the inside the only way?  I was throwing around the idea of using the bedliner material you can buy for trucks.  Would this not hold well or crack with the flex?  This would be a very cheap and fast way to sturdy it up, and put a nice texture on the underside.  Opinions?<P>A Getrag 5-speed with the 3.4, is the stock diff gonna be able to hold up to this?  Or, is it better to upgrade at that point?  Or is it a totally new diff to fit the 3.4?<P>T.I.A.<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'70 BMW 2002<BR>'57 Chevy BelAir||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-01-2001||10:40 AM||||pretty sure Pisa just acts as a clearing house for parts. Dont think they actually manufacture anything. If you have any questions on stuff they have, call them to get the actual suppliers number and ask direct. I havent heard any complaints here, and Ive bought lots of stuff from them myself.<BR><P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/rogergarrison1.gif"> ||||reg||1
